    {
      "id": "claim_fbab39b173f04969a390f84b46fb90f2",
      "statement": "In courses/routers.py, the /recommended endpoint is registered on public_router ahead of GET /{course_id} specifically because FastAPI matches routes in registration order and public_router is included before the authenticated router in routers.py; without this ordering FastAPI would try to parse 'recommended' as an integer course_id and return 422. The /recommended endpoint itself still requires an authenticated user via require_role(\"user\").",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/src/courses/routers.py#L59-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:deb577fef53175e32e82bbe5a1106326bd191745d22ceae1b1cdc1d33b4e4662:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_42b4fb47ad8943fa84d745f445c2fc12",
      "statement": "api.dependencies.require_role(min_role) is a FastAPI dependency that compares the current user's role against a fixed ROLE_HIERARCHY (user < lector < guarantor < superadmin) and raises 403 if the user's role level is below the required minimum; it internally depends on auth.get_current_user.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/dependencies.py#L235-L254",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2a3d050e9a69da882d38e850eaa76137fca4e2ec288cb7c9b1868ba396e2b671:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a11d4bce88174c2695ae27191bb4f340",
      "statement": "api/authorization.py provides three ownership-based authorization helpers used inside controllers for finer-grained checks beyond require_role: validate_ownership (owner or, by default, guarantor/superadmin bypass), validate_owner_or_superadmin (owner or superadmin only, no guarantor bypass), and validate_superadmin (superadmin only); all three 404 via _check_resource_exists if the resource is missing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/authorization.py#L24-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3b56c250145fba9874b057da74aed824a965e939942c5ed9a41e60d1902f7fb1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9a0ef53590e64fb48bd71fc798ab07d0",
      "statement": "api/src/common/utils.py defines get_or_404, which generically loads a row by primary key via SQLAlchemy reflection, raises HTTPException(404) with a model-name-derived default message if missing, and by default also filters is_active.is_(True) when the model exposes that column.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/src/common/utils.py#L42-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:535e59ac92071c375d3f3837667ec929e20df173d47c35406d6fdd2519494ffa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bb0d0c2ef3774bed9abb3d6e35237526",
      "statement": "api/src/common/utils.py defines assert_course_editable, which raises HTTPException(400) unless the course's status is draft, generated, or edited, gating course mutation endpoints to the editable lifecycle stages.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/api/src/common/utils.py#L72-L80",
