    {
      "id": "claim_cb7594b9aa474c7c80b86b62aa730a46",
      "statement": "Each backend domain under api/src/* (and api/src/publicDB/*) follows a routers.py -> controllers(.py or package) -> schemas.py layering convention; simpler domains (modules, enrollments, activities, catalogs, users, superadmin, feedbacks, module_tickets, editor_images, agents) use a single-file controllers.py, while the courses and publicDB.resources domains use a controllers/ package split into per-operation modules (create.py, read.py, update.py, delete.py, plus recommended.py for courses and comment.py for resources) re-exported through controllers/__init__.py.",
